      "mergeID": "609b76de13a52e74b69dbb82",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When I switch the safety setting, the avatar of the corresponding player is reloaded, but the Expression Parameter seems to be out of sync at this time.\nI've tested this and it seems to be the same problem reported at https://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/bug-when-other-players-load-an-avatar-faster-than-the-avatar-wearer-the-expressi When tested, these players play the animation with all parameters set to 0/false, similar to the issue reported on . When the player changes some expression parameter, or when another player joins, it will synchronize and show up correctly. However, avatars that are not designed to have all parameters set to zero in the meantime will appear unintentionally (e.g. without clothes).\nhttps://youtu.be/bqskTT_FgVk",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[BUG] Incorrect parameters are read when changing safety settings",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "60994e625d97441613ffe96b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Additional testing confirmed that the default values of the parameters seem to be loaded, not necessarily 0/false.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
